From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: hci_qca: power the WCN3950 off at hci down

WCN3950 support added the chip to every WCN399x case of the power-on
path (regulators, the 2400 baud power pulses) but to none of
qca_power_off(): "hciconfig hci0 down", or Bluetooth switched off in the
UI, sent no power-off pulse and left the regulators enabled: the chip's
Bluetooth part stayed powered, with the host's UART closed
(HCI_QUIRK_NON_PERSISTENT_SETUP), anything it sent on RX reaching only
the UART's wake-up interrupt, and its idle current drawn for as long as
the phone ran. qca_serdev_remove() skipped it too.

Handle the WCN3950 like the other WCN399x: the power-off pulse at 2400
baud, then the regulators off; the next hci up already goes through
qca_regulator_init() (regulators, port reopened, both pulses), which is
also the first power-on at every boot. The regulators are shared with
the Wi-Fi part of the chip on the F(x)tec Pro1X; regulator_bulk_disable()
only drops Bluetooth's own enable.

The pulse is written only while the port is open, as upstream does now
for the others: qca_close() may power off after hci_uart_close() closed
the port.
---
diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
index d99272451e..0a5c032416 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
@@ -2350,12 +2350,19 @@ static void qca_power_off(struct hci_uart *hu)
 	power = qcadev->bt_power;
 
 	switch (soc_type) {
+	case QCA_WCN3950:
 	case QCA_WCN3988:
 	case QCA_WCN3990:
 	case QCA_WCN3991:
 	case QCA_WCN3998:
-		host_set_baudrate(hu, 2400);
-		qca_send_power_pulse(hu, false);
+		/*
+		 * Both write to the port, which hci_uart_close() may have
+		 * closed already (HCI_QUIRK_NON_PERSISTENT_SETUP)
+		 */
+		if (test_bit(HCI_UART_PROTO_READY, &hu->flags)) {
+			host_set_baudrate(hu, 2400);
+			qca_send_power_pulse(hu, false);
+		}
 		break;
 	default:
 		break;
@@ -2368,6 +2375,7 @@ static void qca_power_off(struct hci_uart *hu)
         }
 
 	switch (soc_type) {
+	case QCA_WCN3950:
 	case QCA_WCN3988:
 	case QCA_WCN3990:
 	case QCA_WCN3991:
@@ -2692,6 +2700,7 @@ static void qca_serdev_remove(struct serdev_device *serdev)
 		of_platform_depopulate(&serdev->dev);
 
 	switch (qcadev->btsoc_type) {
+	case QCA_WCN3950:
 	case QCA_WCN3988:
 	case QCA_WCN3990:
 	case QCA_WCN3991:
